/*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*\
  vlle05_produced_feed  --  a `phaseSet VLLE` decanter whose feed ANOTHER
  unit produced: whose search does that stream mean?

  A STRUCTURAL WITNESS on vlle03's synthetic system (compA, compB, compC:
  not real substances).  Its three component records are ADOPTED copies that
  carry an INVENTED formation datum (dHf_298 = 0, s_298 = 200 for all three)
  so that the energy report runs; only differences of it are read.  No
  number here is a property of any real mixture.

  THE QUESTION.  An unpinned (T, P, z) means its own equilibrium (R-E2), and
  for a feed to a unit that admits a vapour and TWO liquids that equilibrium
  is the three-phase one -- which is why, since DEV.md C35 item 4, a stream
  fed to a VLLE flash is resolved with the flash's own search by the energy
  report and the stream table.  But a PRODUCED stream keeps its PRODUCER's
  answer (CLAUDE.md §3).  `preheater` is a heater: it solves for the outlet
  whose enthalpy is H_in + Q on the VAPOUR-LIQUID surface, and publishes
  `heated` at 352.33 K with vf = 0.0089 -- one liquid and a whisker of
  vapour.  Under the decanter's three-phase search the same (T, P, z) is two
  liquids and a fifth of vapour.

  WHAT WENT WRONG (measured 2026-10-05, before C37 item 4).  The report
  re-read `heated` with the decanter's search while the heater had priced
  it vapour-liquid: the preheater's row left 193.92 kW unattributed and the
  plant's first law missed by -193.92 kW, at exit 0.

  THE RULE (DEV.md C37 item 4).  A stream means its CONSUMER's search only
  when it is an AUTHORED inlet or a three-phase search itself published it
  (`flashState::consumerSearchApplies`).  `heated` is a heater's outlet, so
  the report, the stream table and the decanter's own duty all read the
  state the heater published; the demixing it undergoes in the drum is the
  decanter's duty (169.8 kW at 350 K), and every row closes.

  What to read: the energy balance by unit (both rows close) and the plant
  first law; the decanter's `Q_kW`, which is the cost of bringing the
  heater's vapour-liquid outlet to the drum's three-phase state.
  Gate: check_vlle_fallback arm (f).
\*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

units
(
    {
        name        preheater;
        type        heater;
        in          feed;
        outputs     ( heated );
        operation   { Q  50 kW; }
    }
    {
        name        decanter01;
        type        isothermalFlash;
        model       gibbsMinimisation;      // the machine, NAMED (type -> model -> operation)
        in          heated;
        outputs     ( vapor  liquidA  liquidB );

        operation
        {
            T          350.0 K;
            P          1.0 bar;
            phaseSet   VLLE;
            alphaRich  compA;
            betaRich   compB;
        }
        compositionTol   1e-5;
        maxOuterIter     200;
    }
);
